# ClientFlow engineering standards

ClientFlow is a multi-tenant SaaS client portal showcase. Cursor is the only AI coding assistant for this repository.

## Language

- Talk to the developer in Vietnamese when chatting about this project.
- Write code, comments, commits, and technical docs in clear professional English.

## Architecture

- Prefer feature-oriented modules under `src/features/*` with thin App Router pages.
- Keep Supabase access in `src/lib/supabase/*` using `@supabase/ssr` (no deprecated auth helpers).
- Enforce tenant isolation in PostgreSQL RLS. Application checks are defense-in-depth, not the only gate.
- Do not put `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in client components, public env vars, or browser bundles.

## Security

- Validate inputs with Zod before writes.
- Protect dashboard routes with server-side session validation (`getUser` / `getClaims`).
- Never trust organization IDs from the client without membership verification + RLS.
- Never commit secrets, `.env.local`, or service-role keys.

## Quality bar

- Prefer small vertical slices with acceptance criteria.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and premature abstractions.
- Do not fabricate test results, deployments, or completed features.
- Do not commit, push, change remotes, or deploy unless explicitly asked.

## Day boundaries

- Day 02 foundation: auth, organizations, clients vertical slice, RLS, CI, docs.
- Do not implement Day 03 scope (full project/document management) unless requested.
